## Stack

Next.js (App Router) + React + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4 with a generated Material 3 theme, Radix
Dialog, Vitest + Testing Library, ESLint, Prettier. Scaffolded with `create-buxo-app`.

## Development

Package manager is **pnpm** (not npm; there is no `package-lock.json`).

```bash
pnpm install
pnpm dev              # dev server (Turbopack) on http://localhost:3000
pnpm build            # production build
pnpm test             # vitest, single run (pnpm test:watch to watch)
pnpm lint             # eslint (CI runs it with --max-warnings=0)
pnpm typecheck        # tsc --noEmit
pnpm format:write     # prettier, whole repo
pnpm format:check     # what CI runs
pnpm check            # format check + lint + typecheck + tests, run before pushing
pnpm theme            # regenerate the color theme (see below)
```

### Workflow

- __WORKFLOW__
- CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs tests, the format check, lint, the theme check, type checking, and a
  production build on every PR into `__DEFAULT_BRANCH__` and every push to it.
- Run `pnpm format:write && pnpm check` before pushing, or CI will fail.

## Theme

Colors are Material 3 roles generated by `scripts/generate-theme.mjs`
(using `@material/material-color-utilities`) from the seed colors in `theme.config.json`.

```bash
pnpm theme                                   # regenerate from theme.config.json
pnpm theme --primary "#236488"               # change the primary seed (saved to theme.config.json)
pnpm theme --secondary "#f8b8d5"             # give secondary its own seed instead of deriving it
pnpm theme --secondary none                  # go back to deriving it from primary
pnpm theme --variant vibrant --contrast 0.5  # scheme variant and contrast (-1 to 1)
pnpm theme --check                           # CI: fail if the generated files are stale
```

Seeds: `primary` (required), and optional `secondary`, `tertiary`, `neutral`, `error`.
Variants: `tonal-spot` (default), `fidelity`, `content`, `vibrant`, `expressive`, `neutral`,
`monochrome`, `rainbow`, `fruit-salad`.

It writes two files. **Never edit them by hand**, and commit them together with `theme.config.json`:

- `src/app/theme.css`: the `--md-*` tokens for light and dark, mapped into Tailwind, so every role is a
  utility: `bg-primary`, `text-on-primary`, `bg-surface-container-high`, `border-outline-variant`, ...
- `src/lib/theme-colors.ts`: a few of the same colors as constants for the browser theme-color, the web
  manifest, and the share image.

Always pair a background role with its on-color (`bg-primary` + `text-on-primary`); the generator
guarantees contrast for those pairs. Dark mode follows the system and can be overridden with
`data-theme="light" | "dark"` on `<html>`, which is what `<ThemeToggle>` does. Use `dark:` only for
things the roles don't cover (the roles already switch on their own).

Shape (`rounded-xs` to `rounded-xl`), elevation (`shadow-elev-1..3`), motion (`ease-standard`), and type
(`type-headline-lg`, `type-body-md`, ...) are defined in `src/app/globals.css`. See them all at
`/styleguide`.

## Where things live

| Path                         | What                                                                 |
| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `src/app/`                   | Routes (App Router)                                                  |
| `src/app/styleguide/`        | Every color, type style, and component on one page. Delete when done |
| `src/app/og-image.png/`      | Generated link-preview image. Replace with `public/og-image.png`     |
| `src/app/icon.svg`           | Placeholder favicon. Replace with the real logo                      |
| `src/components/`            | Shared building-block components                                     |
| `src/lib/site.ts`            | Site name, description, author, canonical URL                        |
| `src/lib/navigation.ts`      | The nav items used by the top bar, the drawer, and the footer        |
| `src/lib/metadata.ts`        | `pageMetadata()` for per-page SEO metadata                           |
| `src/lib/structured-data.ts` | schema.org JSON-LD for the site and each page                        |
| `src/lib/fonts.ts`           | The three font roles (brand, ui, body)                               |
| `src/tests/`                 | Vitest tests                                                         |
| `scripts/`                   | Tooling that is not part of the app                                  |

## Building blocks

| Component                         | Use                                                                  |
| --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `Button`, `LinkButton`            | Actions and links that look like buttons. 5 variants, optional icons |
| `IconButton`                      | Icon-only button; the `label` is required                            |
| `Container`                       | Page-width wrapper with responsive margins                           |
| `PageHeader`                      | The `<h1>` of a page, with optional eyebrow and description          |
| `Section`                         | A titled `<section>` with an `<h2>`                                  |
| `Card`                            | Filled, elevated, or outlined; `href` makes the whole card a link    |
| `Tag`                             | Non-interactive label                                                |
| `FilterChip`                      | Toggle with `aria-pressed`                                           |
| `TextField`                       | Labelled input with hint and error wiring                            |
| `ConfirmDialog` (`dialog.tsx`)    | "Are you sure?" dialog that awaits an async action                   |
| `Navbar`, `NavLinks`, `NavDrawer` | Sticky top bar, desktop links with dropdown groups, mobile drawer    |
| `Footer`                          | Site name, nav links, copyright                                      |
| `ThemeToggle`                     | Light/dark switch, remembered in `localStorage`                      |
| `JsonLd`                          | Safely emits a JSON-LD `<script>`                                    |

## Conventions

- **Class names:** `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` (clsx + tailwind-merge). Don't concatenate class strings by hand.
- **Colors:** theme roles only (`bg-primary`, `text-on-surface-variant`), never raw hex or Tailwind's
  default palette, so the theme script stays in control.
- **Imports** use the `@/` alias (`@/components/...`, `@/lib/...`) except for siblings in the same folder.
- **Site constants:** name, description, canonical URL live in `@/lib/site`. Build absolute URLs with
  `absoluteUrl(path)`; don't hardcode the domain.
- **Files** are kebab-case; components are default exports.
- **Client components** only where needed (`'use client'` at the top). Keep pages as server components
  and put interactive parts in a sibling client component (see `src/app/styleguide/demos.tsx`).

### Adding a page (checklist)

1. Create `src/app/<name>/page.tsx` (server component).
2. Define `const PAGE = { title, description, path } satisfies PageInfo` and export
   `metadata = pageMetadata(PAGE)`. **Never write a page's `openGraph`/`twitter` by hand**: Next merges
   metadata shallowly, so you'd drop the shared share image and site fields. Keep the description
   110–160 characters.
3. Render `<JsonLd data={webPageLd(PAGE)} />` after the page content.
4. Add it to `navItems` in `src/lib/navigation.ts` if it belongs in the navigation.
5. Add the route to `src/app/sitemap.ts` (it is a hand-maintained list), or set `noindex: true` for
   unfinished pages.

### Gotchas

- **Hydration / client-only values:** don't `setState` in a `useEffect` just to read `window`,
  `matchMedia`, or `localStorage`. ESLint (`react-hooks/set-state-in-effect`) rejects it. Use
  `useSyncExternalStore` with a server snapshot. See `theme-toggle.tsx` and `top-app-bar.tsx`.
- **Next 16:** `next lint` no longer exists (use `pnpm lint`); middleware is `src/proxy.ts`.
- **TypeScript** stays on 6.x until `typescript-eslint` supports 7 (lint crashes on 7.0).
- **`@material/material-color-utilities`** is pinned to 0.3.0 on purpose: 0.4.0 has ESM imports that
  plain Node can't resolve, which breaks `pnpm theme`.

